ular dependency where T1 cannot release the mutex until T2 finishes, and T2 cannot acquire the mutex to finish.\", \"root_cause\": \"Thread T1 acquires mutex 'state', then calls pthread_join on T2 while still holding the mutex. Thread T2 attempts to lock the same mutex 'state' in its worker function, causing a deadlock as T1 waits for T2 to terminate and T2 waits for the mutex held by T1.\", \"confidence\": 0.95, \"edits\": [{\"file\": \"main.c\", \"search\": \"pthread_mutex_lock(&state); puts(\\\"T1 LOCK state\\\"); shutdown_requested=1;\\n    pthread_create(&t,NULL,worker,NULL); pthread_barrier_wait(&ready);\\n    puts(\\\"T1 WAIT worker_exit\\\"); pthread_join(t,NULL); pthread_mutex_unlock(&state);\", \"replacement\": \"pthread_mutex_lock(&state); puts(\\\"T1 LOCK state\\\"); shutdown_requested=1;\\n    pthread_mutex_unlock(&state);\\n    pthread_create(&t,NULL,worker,NULL); pthread_barrier_wait(&ready);\\n    puts(\\\"T1 WAIT worker_exit\\\"); pthread_join(t,NULL);\"}], \"reasoning_summary\": \"T1 locks state, starts T2, waits at barrier, then tries to join T2 while still holding state lock. T2 needs state lock to proceed. Moving mutex unlock before thread creation allows T2 to acquire the lock, complete its work, and terminate so T1 can successfully join it.\", \"expected_effect\": \"Eliminates the circular wait by ensuring T1 does not hold the 'state' mutex while waiting for T2 to terminate, allowing T2 to acquire the mutex, complete, and exit so T1 can join it successfully.\", \"risk_notes\": [\"Moving the unlock earlier may reduce critical section length, but since shutdown_requested is set before unlock and accessed by T2 under the same mutex, proper ordering is preserved. No loss of synchronization correctness.\"]}","status":"SUCCESS","latency_ms":3589.0207000193186,"input_tokens":2278,"output_tokens":477,"estimated_cost_usd":null,"verification_status":"PASSED","verification_reason":"The patch passed the configured verification campaign.","verification_evi